  "faq_heading": "Burnaby schools: your questions answered",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The BC Ministry of Education and Child Care school list shows 68 schools with a Burnaby street address: 58 public schools and 10 independent schools. It also shows 5 college and university campuses. In that list, 12 schools marked as offering French Immersion, 4 alternate programs and 1 online school."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public schools here are run by School District 41 (Burnaby). Count by district: School District 41 (Burnaby): 58."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Alternate programs, continuing education centres and online schools that have a street address sit under \"other public schools and programs\"; the level of every school is read from its name."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Public secondary schools with a Burnaby address: Alpha Secondary, BC Provincial School for the Deaf Secondary, Burnaby Central Secondary, Burnaby Mountain Secondary, Burnaby North Secondary, Burnaby South Secondary, Burnaby Youth Hub Secondary Program and Byrne Creek Community Secondary and 6 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Ministry file marks these Burnaby schools as offering French Immersion: Alpha Secondary, Armstrong Elementary, Aubrey Elementary, Brantford Elementary, Cariboo Hill Secondary, Cascade Heights Elementary, Moscrop Secondary, Sperling Elementary, Westridge Elementary and École Inman Elementary and 2 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Independent schools listed for Burnaby include Burnaby Montessori School, Deer Lake SDA School, Holy Cross Elementary School, John Knox Christian - Elementary Campus, Our Lady of Mercy and St. Francis de Sales and 4 more."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Before an offer, ask the district which school serves the exact street address."
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The Burnaby school district publishes its catchments as maps (PDF files), not as a list of streets. Use the district's own page to check an address:",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "Burnaby school district catchments and school finder",
      "h": "https://burnabyschools.ca/elementary-school-addresses/",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
    {
      "t": "p",
      "text": "The district's own school pages also list French Immersion at Capitol Hill Elementary, where the Ministry file flag reads No. Confirm the program with the school before relying on either.",
      "gen": "schools-sup"
    },
